## 650 [WG10], unit 1: continue a lesson video where the student stopped

**Problem.** A student who leaves a hosted lesson video part way comes back to 0:00. The video forgets their speed, and the screen goes dark while they watch (the item's Google Play sample of Whop reviews, read on 5 November 2026).

**What changes, for a signed-in student with access to the course** (components/lesson-player.tsx, lib/lesson-position-rules.ts):
- **Coming back:** "You stopped at 12:40 last time." appears above the video, with two buttons: "Continue at 12:40" and "Start over". Nothing jumps on its own. Either choice moves focus to the video.
- **Speed:** the speed the student chose is used again in the next lessons.
- **Screen:** stays on while the video plays (Screen Wake Lock) where the browser allows it. Without it, the video plays the same.
- **Where the place is kept:** in the browser's own storage, under the course, the lesson and the student's learner key (`emailKey`, a hash). It is never kept for the creator or a visitor. Another student on the same device never sees it.
- **When it is written:** at most once every 15 seconds while playing, and on pause or when the page is left.
- **When it is forgotten:**
  - when the video is watched to its last 10 seconds;
  - on "Start over";
  - after 90 days;
  - for the whole course, once the course page sees that the signed-in student's access is not open. That covers a refund, a lost dispute, an ended membership and being taken off (components/forget-lesson-positions.tsx).

**Design approved by Claude 4 (C4-20261105-2205-C2-9).**
- Storage reads and writes are inside try/catch. With storage blocked, the video plays the same and nothing is offered.
- A place read back must be a whole number of seconds, written in the past and within KEEP_DAYS. It is not offered within 10 s of the video's end.
- The words never say the place follows to another device.

**Cost (MR):** zero on our side. Nothing is sent to the server, so there are no new commands, requests or stored data. No line in tests/plan-cost-registry.ts changes and no price, limit or gate moves. Cross-device sync on the server is unit 2, priced before it is switched on.

**Not in this unit:**
- the video service's player in an iframe (stream), whose position needs its player API;
- the lesson list with durations and time left;
- "Continue where you left off" in the library.

These are unit 2.

## Tests
- RED `e35a860e`: tests/wg10-lesson-position.test.ts fails on its parent (the modules are missing). Fix `998a3f24`: 32/32.
- **Real Chromium** (Playwright, a synthetic 60-second WebM, the bundled component), 14/14:
  - nothing offered on the first visit;
  - pause at 40 s writes 40;
  - speed 1.5 kept and used again;
  - the offer comes back with 0:40, in a group named "Where you stopped";
  - Tab reaches "Continue at 0:40" first; Enter goes to 40 s, removes the offer and focuses the video;
  - "Start over" goes to 0, removes the place and focuses the video;
  - 55 s of 60 offers nothing;
  - another student's place is never read;
  - the course page's forgetting removes only this student's places in this course;
  - with storage blocked, no error and nothing offered;
  - no page errors.
- Linked tests: the 20 test files that read the lesson or course page or the course words pass, accessibility-inventory included (regenerated with the 2 new components). tsc and eslint are clean.

## Acessibilidade
- **Checked:**
  - 2.1.1 keyboard (real Tab/Enter in Chromium);
  - 2.4.3 focus order (the offer comes before the video; the choice focuses the video);
  - 3.2.5 change on request (nothing jumps on its own);
  - 4.1.2 name and role (two native buttons in a group named "Where you stopped");
  - 1.4.6 contrast (white text on black, 21:1; the buttons use the store's checked `st-btn`);
  - 2.5.5 target size (`.btn`, 44 px);
  - 2.2.3 no timing;
  - 3.1.2 language (the store's language, 7 languages written).
- **Steps for the main task (going back to where they stopped):** before, open the lesson, then find the spot by dragging or seeking (several actions and a guess). After, open the lesson and press Continue: 1 step and 1 decision.
- **Not checked:** real screen readers, voice control, Wake Lock on a real phone (headless Chromium does not grant it), and tests with people (item 202).

